** Two arc length steps and one without: in the first step the tip load grows until the tip has moved down by 0.125;
** the second step adds the same change of the tip load on top of the load reached -- every arc length step scales its
** own reference load from zero, starting from the loads the step before ended with -- until the tip has moved down by
** 0.25; the third step holds every load. The end of the second step is the state the model reaches under NIST with the
** tip displacement prescribed, and the third step leaves it there (tests/test_arclength_load_parameter.py).

*include, input=../ArcLengthPenaltyConstraint/model.inp

*solver, solver=NISTPArcLength, name=theSolver

*step, solver=theSolver
startInc=0.1, maxInc=0.1, minInc=1e-6, maxNumInc=100, maxIter=25, stepLength=1
>>options, name=theSolver, arcLengthController=tipDisplacement
>>indirectcontrol, name=tipDisplacement, dof1='model.nodeSets["gen_rightTop"][0].fields["displacement"]', cVector1='0, 1', dof2='model.nodeSets["gen_leftBottom"][0].fields["displacement"]', cVector2='0, 0', L=-0.125
>>dirichlet, name=clamp, nSet=gen_left, field=displacement, 1=0.0, 2=0.0
>>nodeforces, name=tipLoad, nSet=gen_rightTop, field=displacement, 2=-1.0
>>bodyforce, name=selfWeight, elSet=gen_all, forceVector='0.0, -0.005', f(t)='1'

** the controlled quantity's absolute target, and another change of the tip load on top of the one reached
*step, solver=theSolver
startInc=0.1, maxInc=0.1, minInc=1e-6, maxNumInc=100, maxIter=25, stepLength=1
>>indirectcontrol, name=tipDisplacement, dof1='model.nodeSets["gen_rightTop"][0].fields["displacement"]', cVector1='0, 1', dof2='model.nodeSets["gen_leftBottom"][0].fields["displacement"]', cVector2='0, 0', L=-0.25
>>nodeforces, name=tipLoad, 2=-1.0

*step, solver=theSolver
startInc=0.5, maxInc=0.5, minInc=1e-6, maxNumInc=100, maxIter=25, stepLength=1
>>options, name=theSolver, arcLengthController=off
